      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi Greg,\n\nThis variable is created by preprocessing from cgroup_subsys.h features.\n\nFile include/linux/cgroup_subsys.h define:\n```\nSUBSYS(memory) \n```\nAnd then been proprocessed into `memory_cgrp_subsys_on_dfl_key` in `kernel/cgroup/cgroup.c`:\n```\n 132 #define SUBSYS(_x)                \\\n 133   DEFINE_STATIC_KEY_TRUE(_x ## _cgrp_subsys_enabled_key);     \\\n 134   DEFINE_STATIC_KEY_TRUE(_x ## _cgrp_subsys_on_dfl_key); \\ # here create this key\n 135   EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(_x ## _cgrp_subsys_enabled_key);      \\\n 136   EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(_x ## _cgrp_subsys_on_dfl_key);\n```\n\nThe patch of http://go/pa-kernel-src/+/9a84bb13816fe have a call to `sk_under_memory_pressure`. So it\u0027s mandatory to export the this key in allow list.",
